================================================================================
eXSpy and HyperSpy (EDX spectroscopy)
================================================================================

The X-ray line table (Sources/SpectroEDX/Spectroscopy/XRayLineData.swift: line
energies from Chantler 2005, relative line weights from the EPQ library, both as
eXSpy ships them), the detector line-width law, the integration and background
window rules, the spectrum fit and Cliff-Lorimer quantification are ported from
eXSpy, with HyperSpy's channel rounding and slicing. They are compared against
it and carry inline DEVIATION notes where this implementation departs. Agreement
with eXSpy is not validation.

    eXSpy - https://github.com/hyperspy/exspy, commit 7185a4d1
    Copyright (C) 2007-2026 The eXSpy developers
    HyperSpy - https://github.com/hyperspy/hyperspy, version 2.4.0
    Copyright (C) The HyperSpy developers
    Both licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later

The element table in Sources/SpectroEDX/Spectroscopy/Quant/QuantElementData.swift
(atomic weights and densities) comes from eXSpy's elements data (GPL-3.0-or-later).

The Velox EMD reader follows rosettasciio's (https://github.com/hyperspy/rosettasciio,
commit 049e7d70, GPL-3.0-or-later) reading of the format and is compared with it.

The DM4 EELS spectrum-image reader (DM4Experiment.readEELSSpectrumImage) takes E0, the convergence and the
collection semi-angle from the tags rosettasciio's digitalmicrograph reader maps (rsciio/digitalmicrograph/_api.py,
commit 049e7d70) and is compared with rosettasciio's reading of the same files (tools/eels-reader/truth.py).
Tests/SpectroKitTests/Fixtures/rsciio-EELS_SI.dm4 is rosettasciio's public test file
rsciio/tests/data/digitalmicrograph/3D/EELS_SI.dm4 (sha256 f9b8203f384cc355437594b649d4ea3a12cddeb231ebb65508a841a379fa171a,
commit 049e7d70), copied byte for byte as a test fixture under rosettasciio's GPL-3.0-or-later; who recorded its
data is not stated by rosettasciio. The two .truth.json files beside it are rosettasciio's readings of
rsciio-EELS_SI.dm4 and of eels-planted.dm4 (written by tools/eels-reader/make_planted.py, no third-party data).


================================================================================
SciPy, NumPy, HyperSpy and eXSpy (EELS thickness, SpectroEELS)
================================================================================

SpectroEELS ports eXSpy's log-ratio thickness (commit 7185a4d1: the elastic-scattering threshold and intensity,
estimate_thickness, Iakoubovskii's inelastic mean free path and its angular correction), HyperSpy 2.4.0's axis
rounding and slicing (GPL-3.0-or-later, both credited above), SciPy 1.18.1's Savitzky-Golay derivative
(scipy/signal/_savitzky_golay.py and _polyutils.py) and NumPy 2.5.4's gradient and pairwise summation, so that its
results equal eXSpy's. They are compared against it (tools/eels-thickness); agreement with eXSpy is not validation.
Tests/SpectroEELSTests/Fixtures/exspy-linescan-*.f64 are eXSpy's simulated test data
(exspy/tests/signals/data/EELS_*_linescan_simulated_thickness_variation.hspy), GPL-3.0-or-later.

