from M. O. Krause, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 8, 307 (1979), as tabulated in EPQ;
third-party measured data carried with its citation, its own terms unverified - a
recorded risk like FFAST below).

FFAST: the mass absorption coefficients inside EPQ are the FFAST tabulation (NIST
Standard Reference Database 66, Chantler et al.); their own terms were flagged as
unclear by mac4DSTEM's v5.0 research and are carried here as a recorded risk.


================================================================================
HDF5 (not distributed)
================================================================================

The Velox reader calls HDF5 (https://www.hdfgroup.org/, copyright The HDF Group and
the Board of Trustees of the University of Illinois, BSD-style license) through
dlopen at run time. SpectroKit neither links nor ships libhdf5: the host application
supplies it (mac4DSTEM embeds HDF5 2.1.1 with libaec/libsz in its bundle) and carries
its notice. The license texts are kept in Licenses/ for hosts and for the library's
own tests: Licenses/HDF5-LICENSE.txt, Licenses/libaec-LICENSE.txt.
